  "question": {
    "text": "In an electromagnetic system, a quantity defined as the ratio of electric dipole moment and magnetic dipole moment has dimension of $\\left[M^P L^{\\circ} \\mathrm{T}^{\\mathrm{R}} \\mathrm{A}^{\\mathrm{S}}\\right]$. The value of P and Q are :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "amEuv",
      "text": "$-1,0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8MLce",
      "text": "$-1,1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4fkfa",
      "text": "$1,-1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GffZO",
      "text": "$0,-1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electric dipole moment $(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{P}})=\\mathrm{q} \\times 2 \\ell$<br/>Magnetic dipole moment $(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{M}})=\\mathrm{IA}$<br/>$\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{P}}{\\mathrm{M}}\\right]=\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{LTA}}{\\mathrm{~L}^2 \\mathrm{~A}}\\right]=\\mathrm{L}^{-1} \\mathrm{~T}=\\mathrm{M}^0 \\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\mathrm{~T}^1 \\mathrm{~A}^0$<br/>After compering values of $\\mathrm{P} \\& \\mathrm{Q}$ are $0,-1$ Correct Answer : Option 4",
    "image": null
  },
